    "better-accessibility": "Keyboard, focus and accessible semantics. Excludes change/regression reviews. Reviews and fixes keyboard and focus behavior, ARIA, accessible names, forms, screen-reader announcements, motion and zoom in your project against WCAG 2.2. Use directly for current-state w",
    "better-colors": "Palettes, color tokens and contrast. Excludes change/regression reviews. Helps you build and check a color system for your project. It generates palettes, names semantic tokens, converts between formats and measures contrast. Use directly for current-state work and ",
    "better-interface": "UI change/regression reviews: load ONLY this skill in the first call, then stop. Returns the explicit change-review command for staged/index, working/uncommitted, branch, PR and commit ranges, even when a domain is named. Also coordinates current-screen audits.",
    "better-layout": "Responsive layout and reading order. Excludes change/regression reviews. Helps with grouping, alignment, reading order, responsive structure and room for translated text, so a layout holds up when it is resized, translated or mirrored. Use directly for current-state",
    "better-typography": "Typography, fonts and text wrapping. Excludes change/regression reviews. Sets and reviews how text renders in your product, from the type scale and spacing to font features, wrapping, truncation and punctuation. Use directly for current-state work and requested fixe",
    "better-ui": "Surfaces, icons and animation. Excludes change/regression reviews. Polishes the surfaces, icons and motion in your project with exact values for border radius, optical alignment, shadows, icon states and animation. Use directly for current-state work and requested ",
    "better-writing": "Interface copy and error messages. Excludes change/regression reviews. Writes and reviews your interface copy, from labels and errors to empty states and confirmations, so it matches your product's voice and tells people what to do next. Use directly for current-s",
    "build-design": "Builds an approved browser prototype, Markdown screen specification, Figma frame or design image with the project's existing tokens and components. Use when asked to implement a supplied design.",
    "design-browser": "Collect browser evidence for interface work. Use for reference browsing, rendered inspection, interaction QA, performance measurements or design comparison. Default to Playwright CLI; use Aside for research and general browsing.",
    "information-architecture": "Organize product content into destinations, labels and navigation. Use when mapping information architecture, a sitemap or findability from an agreed product brief, or restructuring an existing information hierarchy.",
    "user-flow": "Specify a product task's actions, transitions and recovery paths before implementation, including unanswered requests, interruption, exit and return. Use this skill directly for flow planning; do not load state-machine unless the user explicitly invokes that separa",
    "wireframe": "Turn agreed task flows and content into low-fidelity interactive screens and a Markdown screen specification. Use when deciding screen hierarchy, controls and responsive order before visual design or production implementation."
